# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: type-symbols-print-lowercase-on-autocad — AutoCAD prints (type v) of a VARIANT / SAFEARRAY in lower case
#+STATUS: BLOCKED
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: divergence
#+DEPENDS: a CAD run of probes/sources/probe-type-symbols.lsp on AutoCAD and BricsCAD
#+BRANCH: fix-type-symbols-print-lowercase-on-autocad
#+DATE: 2026-10-08

* Observation

intersectwith-probe.lsp prints =(vl-princ-to-string (type v))=:

| target                         | variant   | its safearray |
|--------------------------------+-----------+---------------|
| AutoCAD 2022 (job 17029587295) | variant   | safearray     |
| BricsCAD V25 / V26             | VARIANT   | SAFEARRAY     |
| clautolisp (any dialect)       | VARIANT   | SAFEARRAY     |

=(eq (type v) 'VARIANT)= is true on AutoCAD all the same (the probe takes
that branch), so the symbol is the same and only its printed name differs.
VLA-OBJECT prints in upper case on AutoCAD too.

* Proposal

Measure which TYPE results AutoCAD prints in lower case (variant,
safearray, maybe others) with vl-princ-to-string, prin1, princ and
vl-symbol-name; if confirmed, print them that way under the AutoCAD
dialects (a divergence to classify per AGENTS.md).

* Status (2026-10-22)

Not implemented: the measured evidence is not enough to decide WHAT to
change. The only AutoCAD datum is one row of intersectwith-probe.lsp
(job 17029587295): =(vl-princ-to-string (type v))= is "variant" /
"safearray". probe-results/autocad/ holds no transcript of that run, and
nothing measures:

- =vl-prin1-to-string= and =vl-symbol-name= of those TYPE results, i.e.
  whether the symbol's NAME is lower case (then =vl-symbol-name=, =strcat=
  of it and =read= round trips all change) or only its printed form;
- whether the literal symbol (='VARIANT=, =(read "VARIANT")=) prints in
  lower case too on AutoCAD, i.e. whether the symbol is interned with a
  lower-case name everywhere, independently of TYPE;
- the other TYPE results (PICKSET, FILE, SUBR, USUBR, EXRXSUBR, INT, REAL,
  STR, SYM, LIST). VLA-OBJECT and ENAME are known upper case on AutoCAD
  (the observation above; block-walk probe, run 20261003T130228Z).

The BricsCAD side is likewise vl-princ-to-string only.

New probe suite: probes/sources/probe-type-symbols.lsp, registered in
probes/sources/manifest.txt (=make probe=, or =PROBE_SUITES=type-symbols=).
For every kind of value it records vl-princ-to-string, vl-prin1-to-string
and vl-symbol-name of =(type v)=, and whether it is EQ to the upper-case
symbol read back; for each type name, how the literal symbol prints (upper
and lower case spellings, quoted in source) and atoms-family of VARIANT /
SAFEARRAY. Checked under clautolisp (--dialect autocad-2022): every row
runs, all upper case.

Next: run it on AutoCAD 2022 and BricsCAD V26, commit the results under
probe-results/, then implement exactly what they show under the AutoCAD
dialects (printer only vs symbol name), with the --strict portability
handling used for comparable divergences and a "*** clautolisp" note on
the TYPE page of the specification.
